{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Rephaim were counted, etc.</b> One needs to know for what purpose the verse informs us that the Rephaim were counted, etc. It appears that since among the nations that HaShem said to Abraham He would give to us (Genesis 15:18), He mentioned the Rephaim as one of the ten, the verse informs us that the land that He gave as an inheritance to the children of Lot is the Rephaim of whom HaShem spoke to Abraham. And this is His saying <b>The Emim dwelt therein formerly</b>, etc., and the meaning of \"formerly\" is before HaShem forged a covenant with Abraham, and the intention in this is that it stand to our merit."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:29.683510381Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}